---
/* The question that opens a case study, optically aligned to the column.

   The box edges already line up: the lede and the paragraph under it both
   start at the same x. What does not line up is the INK, because a capital's
   left side bearing differs from letter to letter, so two questions beginning
   with different letters do not start at the same place even though their
   boxes do.

   The table is the measured bearing of each capital, taken from the rendered
   font with TextMetrics.actualBoundingBoxLeft at 44px and divided by the font
   size, so it holds at any lede size. Positive means ink sits left of the
   origin and the line has to move right by that much.

   Re-measured for Figtree on 2026-11-26, when the lede moved off the display
   serif. The previous table was Instrument Serif italic's, whose bearings
   ranged -0.055 to +0.152 and changed sign between letters — which is why this
   mechanism exists at all. Figtree's never change sign and span only 0.082em,
   but that is still 2.8px at 34px, so the correction is worth keeping. Leaving
   the serif's numbers in place was pushing the signage question 4.3px right
   and the SaveEat one 2.7px left.

   The constant is the body face doing the same thing: Figtree's capitals
   average 1.07px of ink to the RIGHT of their origin at 18px, so the lede is
   lined up to where the paragraph's ink actually starts rather than to its box.

   Re-measure BOTH if --font-text ever changes again.
*/
const BEARING_EM = {
  A: -0.009, B: -0.089, C: -0.043, D: -0.089, E: -0.089, F: -0.089, G: -0.043,
  H: -0.089, I: -0.089, J: -0.007, K: -0.089, L: -0.089, M: -0.089, N: -0.089,
  O: -0.043, P: -0.089, Q: -0.043, R: -0.089, S: -0.048, T: -0.012, U: -0.079,
  V: -0.009, W: -0.009, X: -0.01, Y: -0.009, Z: -0.044,
};
const BODY_INK_PX = 1.07;

const { text } = Astro.props;
const first = String(text ?? '').trim().charAt(0).toUpperCase();
const bearing = BEARING_EM[first];
/* An unlisted opener (a digit, a quote mark) gets no correction rather than a
   guessed one: no shift is a smaller error than the wrong shift. */
const indent = bearing === undefined ? undefined : `text-indent:calc(${bearing}em + ${BODY_INK_PX}px)`;
---
<p class="lede" style={indent}>{text}</p>
